  python  hypothesis.strategies.characters
  haskell arbitraryUnicodeChar, arbitraryASCIIChar, arbitraryPrintableChar
  note    an alphabet is a text whose characters, of any width, are drawn simplest first; any character draws edges of every UTF-8 width, the zero character, a combining mark, a right-to-left override and the last scalar value, then printable ASCII, the Basic Multilingual Plane or any plane, `0` the simplest as in Hypothesis; surrogates never, a `str` holding UTF-8

